    (v_topic_id, 'A 27-day-old infant is brought to the clinic for unilateral left clubfoot (talipes equinovarus). The parents ask about the treatment plan. According to the Ponseti method, the deformities are corrected with serial casting in a specific sequence. Which component of the deformity is corrected LAST?', '["Varus", "Equinus", "Cavus", "Adductus", "Supination"]'::jsonb, 1, 'In the Ponseti method for clubfoot, the CAVE deformities are corrected sequentially: Cavus (elevating the first ray), Adductus, Varus, and finally Equinus. The equinus correction often requires a percutaneous Achilles tenotomy.'),
